#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Nightspire: the storming of the Witch-King's citadel.  A fantasy game
for the Grognard engine.

Men, elves and dwarves march together on Nightspire, the citadel of
Malgrith the Witch-King, while his orcs, trolls and walking dead march
the other way to burn Aldermere.  Malgrith and two of his captains are
sorcerers, and the spell they like best turns a regiment, or a hero,
into a sheep.  Play either side against the computer, or against a
friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./nightspire (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.nightspire.json.  ./nightspire --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

